/T (VAT Fraud often extends beyond national borders, making it increasingly difficult for governments to address cross-border schemes and transactions without cooperation from other nations. Fraudulent businesses can exploit differences in national tax systems, gaps in reporting or different technological advances. On the other hand, an increase in information sharing may raise questions about digital sovereignty and data protection.)
/E (VAT Fraud often extends beyond national borders, making it increasingly difficult for governments to address cross-border schemes and transactions without cooperation from other nations. Fraudulent businesses can exploit differences in national tax systems, gaps in reporting or different technological advances. On the other hand, an increase in information sharing may raise questions about digital sovereignty and data protection.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [11]
>>
